[stderr] +## Mechanical release checks
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The editorial validator must derive, rather than trust, the following report
[stderr] +from published card records and their provenance/review records:
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Check | Required result |
[stderr] +| --- | --- |
[stderr] +| ID/boundary | Exactly 48 unique IDs, exactly `QB-A-01…48`, exactly four named batches of 12; no extra QB-A card. |
[stderr] +| Category | World tournament history, domestic league moments, club/manager/identity, and players/records each equal 12. |
[stderr] +| Difficulty | Each category contains exactly four band-1, four band-2, and four band-3 cards. |
[stderr] +| Format | Each named batch contains exactly three FO, three TF, three OP, and three TA cards; therefore the release has 12 of each format. |
[stderr] +| Competition | No `competitionScopes` value appears on more than six cards: the declared maximums are FIFA World Cup 6, UEFA European Championship 3, Copa América 3, Premier League 6, LALIGA 4, Serie A 4, UEFA Champions League 6, and European Cup 4. |
[stderr] +| Club | No `clubIds` value appears on more than four cards: Liverpool, Barcelona, and AC Milan each appear four times; other cards have no club quota participant. |
[stderr] +| Eligibility | Every card is `published`, has all grammar fields, a resolvable provenance record with a checked date, no unresolved conflict, two distinct accepted reviews of its current revision, and no withdrawal. |
[stderr] +| Originality/accessibility | Every card has accepted originality and accessibility/copy review findings, required text equivalents, and no player-facing copied/source text. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The sample inventory intentionally remains `draft` until per-card research and
[stderr] +review are completed. Thus it is bounded and independently auditable now, while
[stderr] +the validator will correctly reject it as a shippable package until its
[stderr] +provenance and both reviews are supplied.
